spans.s:
√grath or granth (grathnā́ti; granthiṣyáti;
grathitá; -gráthya). --1. string
together, connect;
 —2. put together, i. e.
com-pose (a literary work). [for mgs, cf.
Lat. com-pōnere, ‘put together, compose’;
also serere, ‘connect, entwine,’ w. sermo,
‘discourse.’]

√gras (grásate; jagrasé; ágrasīt; grasiṣyáte;
grastá; grasitvā́; grasyáte;
grāsáyati). --1. swallow; devour, 10^10;
 —2. of the demon Rāhu, who swallows,
i. e. eclipses sun and moon, 23^1. [perhaps
akin w. √2gṛ, ‘swallow.’]
